From b3dd474a2bb5fb99ab1a6a3d7575c62703d8affc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arbicore-eng <eng@arbicore.local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:43:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(flash): B1 six-chain exact-size sizing + B2
 discovery-queue chain fairness

B1 (composition.py): wire the canonical live flash-loan scanner to the EXISTING
generalized six-chain exact-size sizer (build_multichain_price_source/_H05_CHAINS
/build_h05_borrow_sizer/ExactSizeBorrowSizer) via new async helper
_build_live_h05_borrow_sizer, preserving the live Base feed instance. Non-Base
chains (Ethereum,...) now reach exact-size quoting -> Gate 7 instead of
size_basis=probe -> size_not_quoted. Fail-closed/env-gated; no parallel
architecture; sync non-canonical seam left Base-only by design.

B2 (discovery_queue.py, models/discovery.py): DiscoveryQueue.claim_batch now
fills the batch round-robin across chains with eligible candidates (additive
top-level 'chain' field + index; upsert stamps it from hint_metric/subject_id).
Each claim keeps the identical atomic eligibility predicate, expiry semantics,
claim locking and verified_outcome behaviour. Legacy rows (no chain) stay
claimable via the None bucket. No opportunity forced; no downstream gate touched.

Tests: test_emergent_b1_multichain_sizing (7), test_emergent_b2_discovery_queue_fairness (8).
Unchanged: $25 gate, $100k TVL floor, risk/safety gates, Polygon, Network/RPC
config, quoter.py. No deploy/SHADOW/PAPER/LIVE/signing/broadcast.
